WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.660
TOMI STATION

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.370
I'll be on the training arriving at 12:13.
I'm waiting for you by the gate.
Okay.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.250
Looks like I got here a little too early.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.790
Sayaka-chan?

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.370
Senpai...

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.040
Long time, no see! Crazy running into you here!

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.370
Uh, yeah.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.040
Are you waiting for someone?

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.370
Yes. A friend of mine is visiting my house today.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.870
That's right. I remember your house
was close to this station.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.290
I'm glad to see you.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:49.540
I really wanted to apologize when you entered
high school, but then you suddenly transferred away.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.950
I'm sorry, Sayaka-chan.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.750
What exactly are you... apologizing for?

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:06.910
You were just an ordinary girl, but then I pressured
you into going out with me and now, I mean...

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:08.410
Mean what?

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:15.500
I mean, if you still find yourself attracted to other girls,
then that must be because of what I did.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:20.500
But if you've gone back to being an ordinary girl,
then I guess there's nothing for me to worry about...

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.200
Please don't concern yourself.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.830
At this point, I find it strange that
I even fell for you in the first place, Senpai.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:31.700
I see.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.080
Well... I am somewhat grateful to you.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:35.830
Huh?

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.580
Touko!

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.160
Sorry to keep you.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.540
Well, then...

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.330
...farewell.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.410
Was she a friend of yours?

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:00.950
Did I interrupt?

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:02.450
No. It's fine.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.040
So, what's up with this?

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:13.080
Um, well, I just got caught up in the moment...
and reacted without thinking.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.250
You never do that. How weird!

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.410
Not that I mind.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.580
What... are you doing?

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.620
Getting payback?

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.000
Now who's being weird?

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.120
What color do you like?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.290
Huh?

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.790
Hydrangeas.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:59.290
Komorebi kirakira yureteru asa no

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.160
Namikimichi

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:12.790
Itsumo no kimi no "ohayou" tte koe ga kikoeru

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.500
Kagi o kaketa glass no hako ni

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:24.500
Nani o kakushite irundarou?

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:30.700
Ugokihajimeta monogatari

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:35.330
Kimi no sekai motto shiritakute

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:41.450
Guuzen fureta sono yubi o

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:46.040
Ima nigittanda

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.540
Tsuyogari mo yowasa mo

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:56.080
Zenbu tsutsunde ageru yo

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:02.120
Gyutto

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:08.790
Here!

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.250
What's the student council doing over there?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.250
Oh, they're training for the competitive relay.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:16.950
The student council is running, too?

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:16.950
Here... ah!

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.870
I'm sorry, Saeki-senpai.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.200
Let's try it again.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.500
Everyone managed to pass the baton just fine,
except Sayaka and Yuu.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.120
Senpai, you're taking off too quickly!

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.040
That's because you're slowing down too much.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.540
Hey, student council! Time's almost up.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.620
Okay!

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.330
Both of you will just have to keep practicing after school.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.950
Hey, Koito-san. Do you not get along with Saeki-senpai?

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:45.080
W-we get along fine!

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:46.540
Sports Day Committee

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:50.120
Next, I will breakdown the schedule and explain
everyone's duties on the day of the actual event.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:56.290
First, we'll be meeting at 7:30 AM to set up all
of the tents and make sure the grounds are clean.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.790
Seems like this is going to wrap up earlier than planned.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.870
All thanks to our awesome president!

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.540
The entrance ceremony will begin at 9 AM

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:05.080
Everyone here must look at Nanami-senpai and
think that she's perfectly capable

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.950
so please make sure your tasks are done by 8:15 AM at the latest.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.620
Parents and family will arrive at 8 AM,

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.450
of managing a big event like this with no problems.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:11.450
so please make sure everything is in place to welcome them.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.200
Probably everyone's convinced
except Saeki-senpai and myself...

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.750
Lastly, I know we've been over this already, but...

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.870
That's all for today. Good work.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.830
Nanami.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:21.750
Yes?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.410
Can I speak to you for a minute?

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:24.450
Sure.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:28.160
You can go ahead without me, everyone.
Good work today.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.620
Thank you very much.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.200
Don't you two have more relay practice to do after this?

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.120
Do you think we should?

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.200
Why bother? It's fine.

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:48.910
I thought you were the type to take things
more seriously, Saeki-senpai.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.830
I do take things seriously, but only when
it's something that's actually important.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.000
I see.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.660
This competitive relay is an event that
the other clubs only do for fun.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.620
Although Touko seems serious about winning first place.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.500
Do you not get along with Saeki-senpai?

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.370
Did you think I was gullible enough to actually buy that?

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.500
Well, goodbye then.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:20.950
Saeki-senpai!

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.080
Um...

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.830
Are you hungry at all?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:42.410
So, is it your first time getting
fast food like this, Saeki-senpai?

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:46.410
As if. What kind of person do you take me for?

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.040
I thought maybe you were too rich for this place.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.620
Not many people can afford to attend
a private all-girls' school like you did.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:57.290
That school isn't nearly as rich and fancy
as everyone makes it out to be.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:00.200
I've been to places like this with other classmates,

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.250
and I regularly go to family restaurants and karaoke, too.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.700
Sorry to disappoint.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.620
Oh, really? I wouldn't have guessed.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.540
What exactly were you expecting?

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:21.790
I must admit, I think it's bad for my image
to have a first-year go out of her way to help me.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.620
Huh?

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:28.370
We haven't been getting along lately, which is
why you're trying to extend an olive branch, right?

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:32.000
I wouldn't put it quite so dramatically.

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:33.120
Oh?

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:42.370
My first impression was that you were more of an
easy-going person, but I can see now that I was wrong.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:48.370
And I thought you would be timid and respectful,
but you're surprisingly surly for a first-year.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:50.580
Although...

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.540
I don't hate people who know how to get to the point.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:56.950
Did you say something?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:57.750
Nothing.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.500
Want to have some?

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:15.910
Saeki-senpai, do you honestly want to perform
the stage show for the culture festival?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.410
On a personal level, I could go either way.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.000
"Either way", huh?

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:28.540
I think it has the potential to be very fun,
but at the same time I'm sure it will be a big burden.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.000
In other words, you're only doing it
because Nanami-senpai wants to?

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.910
If Touko wants to do it, then I'm going to help her.

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:42.000
I think the show will be really impressive if we do it right,

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.000
and besides, she's so stubborn
nobody will ever talk her out of it.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:48.660
Saeki-senpai, she...

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.450
You really like Nanami-senpai, don't you?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:01.200
Of course. She's my closest friend.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.750
That's not... exactly what I meant.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.790
And do you like Touko, too?

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:09.660
Huh?

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:15.040
Um, well, as a Senpai she's pretty great... I think.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:21.790
Naturally. A friend to me and a senpai to you.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.500
What else could she possibly be?

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.540
Thank you very much.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.330
Pedestrian
Crossing

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:40.000
This stage show... is something very important
to Nanami-senpai, right?

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.370
That's because it's the last thing
her older sister left behind.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:51.700
When it's over, I wonder if Nanami-senpai will...
consider dropping the act she always puts on?

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:55.950
Will she finally just be herself?

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:59.410
I don't think that's what Touko actually wants.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.830
If that day comes...

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:08.830
Will I...

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:12.620
be able to tell her how I feel?

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:16.540
What will...

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.040
happen to me?

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.000
What color do you like?

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:35.370
Hydrangeas.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:42.000
Intersection

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:47.080
Rained In

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.870
Be by my side.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.450
Don't have feelings for anyone else!

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:54.290
And don't let your feelings toward me became hate!

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:00.200
I'm pretty sure I know what Nanami-senpai
wanted to say at that moment.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:06.040
"Please don't fall in love with me."

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.500
The rain isn't letting up.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:14.830
It's coming down really hard.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:16.870
Maki-kun.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.580
Didn't bring an umbrella?

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:22.040
Nope, but it's okay because I'm walking home with Akari.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:25.160
Hey, Maki! Did you bring an umbrella?

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.250
Yeah, why?

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.120
Can I cram under it with you?

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.080
You are so helpless.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.410
Well, see you later.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:33.700
Later!

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:38.580
Yuu!

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:40.870
Sorry to keep you.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.410
Is your meeting finished?

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:46.870
Yep. I wish it would stop raining
when we have to practice outside.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:50.410
I'm glad you brought an umbrella today, Akari.

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:51.330
Where's Koyomi?

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:55.120
She went home already. She wanted to work on
the script for the Student Council's stage show.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:58.000
She's been having fun with that lately.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:03.790
Riko-sensei lent us a DVD for reference,
and once she watched that it lit a fire in her.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:07.410
I hope it's sunny on Sports Day.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:08.870
Me too.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.120
Didn't you bring an umbrella?

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.330
I didn't know it was going to rain today!

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.750
I'm just gonna run home.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.040
Cool, see ya.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:24.250
Oh, that must be the Senpai who Akari...

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.080
Go after him.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.330
Huh? But...

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:30.410
I'll figure something out.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.830
What? Really?

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:33.870
Just go.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:41.620
Thank you!

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.250
All righty then.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:58.950
I said I'd figure something out, but...

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:02.540
I'm betting all the people who don't
have club activities already went home.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:10.700
LOANER UMBRELLAS
Please return the

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:10.700
following day 
-The Student Council

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:09.290
Someone without a club,
leaving in the same direction that I am....

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:11.950
LOANER UMBRELLAS
Please return the following day

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.160
Of course...

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:21.580
The Student
Council

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:22.910
Profile
Touko Nanami

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.040
Nah.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.250
Hello?

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.120
Hello, is this Yuu-chan?

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.700
Huh? Oh, Hiro-kun?

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:40.750
Sorry, Rei-chan's driving right now.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:41.830
Oh, really.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:43.870
You forgot your umbrella, didn't you?

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:45.000
Did you hear that?

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.580
Yeah, she's right.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:47.660
I knew it.

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:48.830
Want us to come and pick you up?

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:53.910
No, that's okay. I don't want to interrupt your date,
I'll figure something out.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:54.950
Are you sure?

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:59.330
Yeah. Oh, I just spotted a friend of mine.
Talk to you later!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:00.370
Oh, all right.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.250
Is she okay?

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:05.950
Yeah, she found a friend.

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:08.790
Yuu-chan must have a lot of them at school.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.200
Well, she's always been pretty good at socializing.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.950
And now she's on the student council, too.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:16.160
Although, she struggled to decide whether or not to join.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.540
I didn't know that.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:27.540
Once she starts working on something it's fine,
but she always hesitates to make the initial commitment.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.620
I just hope there's someone who will help pull her along.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:49.950
The rain just won't let up.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:57.080
Whatever. I'll just walk through it.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:57.950
Yuu!

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.250
Yuu.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:06.870
You don't have an umbrella?
Were you just going to go home without one?

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.160
Oh, well...

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:11.580
I'm glad I found you in time.

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:14.950
I tried calling you earlier, but it said the line was busy.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:17.080
Oh, sorry.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:21.540
Let's walk home together!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.330
This is a little nostalgic for me.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:42.540
When I was younger, I used to walk home
with my sister on this road.

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:48.290
She'd always forget her umbrella and
so I would walk all the way to the school to give her one,

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:51.450
but I was stupid and only brought
the one I used with me.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:55.290
You would walk? But isn't
your house pretty far from here?

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:59.370
Oh, I used to live near here until elementary school.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:06.370
If my family hadn't moved, we might
have been in the same middle school.

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:09.790
Maybe so, but I doubt we would have met each other.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.120
Don't be such a downer!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:19.330
You're the only person I can openly talk
about my childhood with, Yuu.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:34.540
Oh! Senpai, I'm sorry I made you
hold the umbrella all this time!

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:35.620
Let me do it!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:36.950
Don't worry about it.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:37.790
But...!

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:40.200
It's easier if the taller person holds it, anyway.

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:42.830
You aren't even that much taller than I am.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:45.000
No, actually, I think I have about 10 centimeters on you.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:48.040
Huh? There's no way it's that much.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.790
I'm 163 centimeters tall, you know.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:57.750
See? Just give it back, the light's already green.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:02.450
No way! Look, you are totally soaked on that side,
Senpai!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.330
Huh?

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:07.700
This is your umbrella, so at least
make sure you keep yourself covered!

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:11.250
But I don't want to see you get wet!

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.450
Don't give me that!

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.000
Jeez...

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.790
Just let me do it, Senpai.

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:23.450
You know, we look so weird right now.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:33.330
I think that's the first time
I've seen you laugh so hard, Yuu.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:34.950
Are you sure?

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:39.250
Well, that must be because whenever
I'm with you it causes me a lot of problems.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.830
It's a problem to be with me?

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:44.870
It's not really a problem.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:49.410
In fact, right now... I think it's pretty fun.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:54.290
The biggest problem is if you were
to catch a cold out here, Senpai.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:58.120
Look, why don't we stop over there for a while?

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:00.000
I'm fine.

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:01.700
Come on, just for a while.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:06.200
Just hold on. I should have a...

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:10.370
Wow, you really come prepared!

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:14.870
That's because someone decided
we have to do Sports Day practice every day.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:18.290
I thought it would be good to bring something
to wipe off all the sweat.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:29.370
We're both the younger sisters in our families,
but you're much better at pampering others than I am.

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:32.250
Stand still please.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:38.950
Okay, just one more time.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:48.330
You're so good at pampering others, which is why
I'm worried I might be... taking advantage of that.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:55.830
I can't help but think you might
be tired of all this, of dealing with me,

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:58.330
and you're just forcing yourself through it.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.290
I'm scared that you'll end up hating me because of it.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:03.830
Are you sure you're okay?

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:12.080
I'd say you pamper me a lot more,
by taking time to ask questions like that.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.830
Maybe this is just a trait that
younger sisters are born with.

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:25.870
Snacks

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:20.950
I'm fine. I don't consider what I do to be "pampering" you.

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:25.870
Actually, you really saved me
when you showed up today.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:28.250
It made me...

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:32.080
...really happy.

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.540
"Really happy"?

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:43.330
What does she mean... by that?

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.500
Oh, nothing!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:54.040
It's just, a lot of other people left me
by the wayside on their way home today.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:57.950
So, when you showed up it was a big relief, Senpai.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:01.620
That's all. I didn't mean anything weird by it!

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:15.910
That sounds more like the Yuu I know.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.330
I'm happy, too.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:26.700
We get to be lovey-dovey under this umbrella.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.910
"Lovey-dovey"...

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:33.830
Putting it that way is pretty embarrassing, no?

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:36.120
Then how else should I put it?

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.620
I don't know...

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:41.120
Hey, Yuu. Let's stay here for a while longer.

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:42.450
Okay?

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:45.040
Fine with me.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.330
Hooray!

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.120
So warm...

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:56.370
I never realized she had such a high body temp.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:59.660
No, maybe mine is just too low.

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:04.750
I want some of her warmth...

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:12.410
But I'm fine for now, just like this.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.120
Senpai, what color do you like?

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:20.830
The hydrangeas...

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:30.450
Good grief.

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:33.450
Nanami-senpai really is...

00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:41.580
Here!

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:44.660
Did we do it?

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:46.120
How were we?

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:49.330
All it took was a little effort and
you two pulled it off flawlessly!

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:53.750
I mean...

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:56.040
...anyone would, if you made them
do it over and over like this.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:59.160
I know you'll just do as well in the actual relay!

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:04.620
Come on, don't slow down there!

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:08.790
You know, Touko can be a real pain sometimes.

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:10.250
Tell me about it.

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.580
Shiritakute shiritakunai

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:22.500
Kono mama de ii (kono mama de ii)

00:22:23.250 --> 00:22:26.120
Maru batsu ga tsuku no nara

00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:32.660
Zutto zutto ashita ni naranaide

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:52.750
Tooi sekai no koto dato omotteita (omotteita)

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:59.620
Watashi ni wa kankei nai konna kimochi (Konna kimochi)

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:01.540
Kimi ni dattara ari kamo ne

00:23:01.540 --> 00:23:03.410
Kokoro no naka o misetemo

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:07.040
Datte kitto kawaranai

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:08.910
Kokoro no ichi ga wakatta yo

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:10.750
Nandaka kurushiku naru yo

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:13.830
Fui ni kawaru kazamuki ga

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:16.450
Ashita wa nani ni naru?

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:18.200
Yagate kimi ni naru

00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:21.830
Sensai na nakami nozoite mite

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:23.750
Moyamoya shiteru

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:25.580
Kimochi ga baretara

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:29.370
Kimi wa nigeteshimau ka na
